# Commercial S10.2D Tailscale route diagnosis — 2026-09-05

## Observed condition

The local Tailscale backend reported `Running`, but the bounded single-packet
probe to the canonical server Tailscale address did not establish a direct
connection. A small client/daemon version skew was also reported. No server,
Telegram, DNS, repository or runtime mutation was attempted.

## Safe hypotheses

1. The existing local session needs re-authentication.
2. The server is reachable only through a relay and the direct-only probe was
   too strict for the current network path.
3. The canonical server peer is temporarily unavailable.

## Read-only diagnostic plan

1. Inspect only the local backend/login state and peer reachability metadata.
2. Attempt one bounded non-interactive SSH identity check with no remote
   mutation and no credential bypass.
3. If authentication is required, include it in the already approved single
   bundled operator checkpoint.
4. Proceed to backup or deployment only after the canonical host identity and
   route are proven.

## Read-only diagnosis result

The canonical peer is known, online and active. A bounded probe allowing the
normal relay-or-direct path succeeded. The initial failure was therefore
caused by requiring a direct connection from a single packet, not by a server
or peer outage. Tailscale SSH then reached the official additional-authentication
gate; host identity has not yet been accepted as proven and remains part of
the single operator checkpoint. The client/daemon version skew is unchanged
and non-blocking for the verified route.

## Rollback and boundary

No rollback is required because no mutable action occurred. Adult media, AVS,
payment, external publishing, Controlled Beta and production remain closed.
